meta {
  name: chat commands
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/commands
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  The one list of chat commands for the terminal REPL and the web chat (card 554), in its order: id, name, sub, aliases, takesArgs, group (chat, playbook, codegraph, skills), surfaces (web, repl, both), developerOnly, wired (false for a row another card owns) and help.en. The web builds its /help, its slash picker and the Skills and Commands page from it.
  
  Fence: host. Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
